   1++09F7              ; =========================================================================
   2++09F7              ; PROJECT 125 — 8086 physical memory backend with BIOS ROM overlay
   3++09F7              ;
   4++09F7              ; Guest RAM below FE000h maps to NeoGS pages 4..67. The 8 KiB BIOS ROM
   5++09F7              ; overlay at FE000h-FFFFFh is read from NeoGS page 75 (offset 0000-1FFF).
   6++09F7              ; Guest writes to the BIOS range are rejected. Page 67 therefore exposes
   7++09F7              ; only FC000h-FDFFFh as writable RAM; its upper half is shadowed by page 75.
   8++09F7              ; Window C000-FFFF is switched through MPAGEX. Resident firmware remains in
   9++09F7              ; WIN0/page 0; WIN2 is reserved for banked firmware overlays. The Z80 stack
  10++09F7              ; is in WIN1/page 3 at #4FFE, below the DMA frame at #5000. MPAGEX never
  11++09F7              ; changes WIN1 or WIN2, so the active stack and banked overlay stay mapped.
  12++09F7              ;
  13++09F7              ; x86_mem_addr is a 20-bit little-endian address:
  14++09F7              ;   +0 = bits 7:0, +1 = bits 15:8, +2 = bits 19:16 (valid 0..0F).
  15++09F7              ;
  16++09F7              ; API:
  17++09F7              ;   x86_mem_init: enable NOROM + EXPAG, preserving other GSCFG0 bits.
  18++09F7              ;   x86_mem_read8:  IN x86_mem_addr; OUT A=value, carry=invalid address.
  19++09F7              ;   x86_mem_write8: IN x86_mem_addr and x86_mem_value; carry=invalid address.
  20++09F7              ;   x86_mem_test: destructive test of the 64-page RAM backing with BIOS overlay.
  21++09F7              ;                 status=0, AX=0001 on pass; status=5, AX=phase:page on fail.
  22++09F7              ;
  23++09F7              ; The test leaves NOROM+EXPAG enabled. It tests the writable guest RAM span,
  24++09F7              ; including the lower 8 KiB of guest page 63; the BIOS overlay is not RAM.
  25++09F7              ; Only WIN3 is switched by MPAGEX;
  26++09F7              ; callers must keep SP in WIN1 and below #5000 for the entire test
  27++09F7              ; (Project124 uses #4FFE, with the stack guard at #4800).
  28++09F7              ; =========================================================================
