   1++8170              ; =========================================================================
   2++8170              ; PROJECT 125 — 8086 real-mode fetch/execute core.
   3++8170              ;
   4++8170              ; Bounded guest execution through CS:IP and the NeoGS physical-memory backend.
   5++8170              ; Implemented groups include: register/immediate and ModR/M MOV, segment MOV,
   6++8170              ; moffs, LEA, XCHG, byte/word ALU and logic, INC/DEC, stack and segment-stack,
   7++8170              ; PUSHF/POPF, LAHF/SAHF, CBW/CWD, flag control, near/far CALL/RET/JMP,
   8++8170              ; short Jcc/LOOP, software interrupts/IRET/INTO, string operations with REP,
   9++8170              ; byte/word IN/OUT, XLAT, WAIT and LOCK-prefix handling.
  10++8170              ; Unsupported instructions still stop with the opcode and CS:IP for diagnosis;
  11++8170              ; this is an expanding 8086-compatible core, not yet a complete PC/XT machine.
  12++8170              ;
  13++8170              ; x86_real_mode_test installs a guest program at 0000:5002 and an interrupt
  14++8170              ; handler at 0000:5100. The guest loads all eight general registers with
  15++8170              ; MOV r16,imm16, invokes INT 20h, then resumes at HLT after handler IRET.
  16++8170              ; The test checks all MOV destinations, interrupt return, FLAGS and SP.
  17++8170              ; Success: status=0, AX=1A02h. Failures: status=9/11 with stage-specific AX codes.
  18++8170              ; =========================================================================
